# incident-console-v2 — build plan

Framework: Next.js (App Router), standalone from v1's Streamlit `incident-console`.

## 1. Structural reference, not a fork

Use `services/ui`'s Turborepo shape (`apps/`/`packages/` split, tsconfig/tailwind/eslint
conventions) as the pattern to follow — it's the only Next.js precedent in this codebase.
Don't drag in the vendored blueprint app itself (`nv-metropolis-bp-vss-ui`) wholesale.

## 2. Components worth copying in directly

- `services/ui/packages/nv-metropolis-bp-vss-ui/dashboard` — clean, only depends on the
  public `@nvidia/foundations-react-core` (Apache-2.0, resolves off npm fine).
- `services/ui/packages/nv-metropolis-bp-vss-ui/video-management`, `alerts` — same, once
  their one `@nemo-agent-toolkit/ui` import is dropped (see next point).
- `services/ui/packages/common/lib-src/utils/chunkedUpload.ts` — copy this one file
  directly (self-contained, no toolkit dependency) instead of installing the toolkit
  for it. Already speaks the exact `mediaFile`+`filename`+`nvstreamer-*` protocol v1's
  `agent_client.py` upload contract uses.

## 3. Chat: build custom, skip the NeMo Agent Toolkit UI package

One `fetch` POST to the agent's `/chat` endpoint (OpenAI-chat-completions shape:
`{messages, model, stream:false, temperature}` in, `choices[0].message.content` out),
state held in a plain `useState` array. No `next-auth`, `idb`, `i18next`, streaming, or
proxy layer — those solve problems v2 doesn't have yet. Upgrade to token streaming later
if response latency actually needs it.

## 4. Backend contract to carry over from v1 (knowledge, not UI code)

- `incident-console/db.py` — authoritative Postgres schema (videos/queries/model_runs/
  incidents + evidence/ground-truth/match/review tables).
- Access pattern: PostgREST over HTTPS (as `services/agent/src/vss_agents/utils/
  incident_db.py` already does), not raw Postgres — `kwanz-ws` blocks port 5432.
- `incident-console/r2_videos.py` — R2/Cloudflare video storage access.
- `../incident-plan/incident-plan-overview.md` — MVP1/MVP2 scope and the
  verification checklist.

## Open items before/while building

- Confirm whether `vss-agent` currently has `/chat` live (vs. only `/generate`) for
  this deployment.
- Decide Postgres access for v2: talk to Supabase/PostgREST directly from Next.js API
  routes, or keep a thin backend layer.
- v1 has heavy lag (Streamlit rerun-on-every-interaction model); v2's plain fetch/React
  approach avoids that class of problem by construction, not by design decision.
